## Customize flags given to the VM: http://erlang.org/doc/man/erl.html
## -mode/-name/-sname/-setcookie are configured via env vars, do not set them here

## SWARM change: the target server is 2 shared vCPUs and 4 GB RAM, and the
## explorer must stay well under 768 MB RSS. The BEAM sizes its scheduler pool
## from the host's core count, not the container's CPU quota, so on a shared
## host it would otherwise start a scheduler per host core and each one carries
## its own run queue and memory. Pin it to two normal and two dirty-CPU
## schedulers. Override with ERL_FLAGS if the box is bigger.
+S 2:2
+SDcpu 2:2

## Two dirty-IO schedulers are plenty: the only IO is HTTP to the node.
+SDio 2

## Collect garbage aggressively rather than trading memory for throughput. The
## workload is many short-lived request processes, so full sweeps are cheap and
## keep the resident set flat between bursts of traffic.
-env ERL_FULLSWEEP_AFTER 10

## Bound the number of concurrent ports; the default 65536 reserves more than
## this service ever needs.
+Q 4096
